    "api_error_status": null,
    "result": "Perfect! The fix is complete and working. Here's what I did:\n\n## The Bug\nThe issue was in `src/money.js` line 13. When converting a decimal price like \"39.95\" to cents, the code was doing floating-point multiplication:\n```javascript\nNumber(Number(s.replace(/,/g, '')).toFixed(2)) * 100\n```\n\nThis resulted in `3995.0000000000005` instead of the expected integer `3995`, causing the validation to fail.\n\n## The Fix\nI replaced that line with:\n```javascript\nMath.round(Number(s.replace(/,/g, '')) * 100)\n```\n\nUsing `Math.round()` properly handles floating-point precision errors. Now `39.95 * 100 = 3995.0000000000005` gets rounded to exactly `3995`.\n\n## Verification\n\u2705 Created and ran a failing test for `parseEuros('39.95')`  \n\u2705 Fixed the bug  \n\u2705 All 50 tests pass  \n\u2705 CLI command now works: `subtrack add Gym 39.95 --since 2026-10-03` \u2713  \n\u2705 Other prices (12.99, 10.99) continue to work correctly\n\nYour gym membership and other subscriptions are now added successfully!",
